# =============================================================================
# ANCHORING RULE -- read before adding anything below.
#
# A gitignore pattern whose only slash is a trailing one matches at EVERY depth.
# So a bare `curated/` matches `src/statarb/curated/` just as readily as the
# top-level data directory -- which is exactly what happened here: the entire
# stage-2 source package (build.py, factors.py, schema.py) was silently
# gitignored and could not be committed. A bare `src/` had the same latent bug
# for the whole source tree.
#
# Therefore: every pattern meant to match ONE specific directory at the repo
# root carries a LEADING SLASH. Verify any new rule with:
#     git check-ignore -v <a source file that must stay tracked>
# which must print NOTHING.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Git keeps every version of every file forever, so a credential committed once
# is effectively public forever even after deletion. Rotate, don't just delete.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx

# ---- Licensed vendor data ---------------------------------------------------
# FactSet and CRSP licences prohibit redistribution, and pushing to GitHub --
# even a private repo -- is redistribution. Data belongs OUTSIDE this repo
# entirely (see FACTSET_DEST_ROOT); these anchored rules are the backstop.
/data/
/raw/
/curated/
/_manifest/
/discovery_output/
/sid_map.parquet
/GICS_Filtered_Cluster_Pairs/
/GICS_Filtered_Equities_Prices/
/GICS_Filtered_Factor_Loadings/
/GICS_Filtered_Factor_Returns/
/GICS_Filtered_Pair_Candidates/
*.duckdb
_delta_log/

# Pickles: nothing in this codebase writes them any more (the pickle-based
# interchange format was replaced by Parquet/Delta). The rule stands as an
# anti-regression guard -- if this ever matches something, question why.
*.pkl

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
develop-eggs/
.eggs/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg

# ---- Virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

# ---- Tool caches ------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# ---- IDE / OS ---------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# =============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED -- each of these was previously ignored and should
# not be, because it blocked something that belongs in version control:
#
#   src/          would gitignore the entire source tree
#   *.csv         blocks committed reference data and test fixtures
#   *.ipynb       blocks notebooks, which are how a result gets demonstrated
#                 (outputs are stripped by nbstripout instead)
#   *.parquet     blocks small committed test fixtures; the anchored data
#                 directories above already cover the real data
#   misc.py       a personal-scratch pattern has no place in a shared repo
#   lib/ lib64/ parts/ var/ downloads/ eggs/
#                 template noise for tooling this project does not use
# =============================================================================
